<p class="mt-align-center"><img alt="The ball-and-stick model in electrostatic potential maps of acetone (ketone) and acetyl chloride (acid chloride). An arrow points toward the carbon atom that is bonded with oxygen." style="width: 525px; height: 253px;" width="525px" height="253px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/478065/6b551e8b4bde2181482987468ba8a2911280c416.png?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=525&amp;height=253" /></p>

<dl>
    <dt><strong class="emphasis bold">Answer</strong></dt>
